    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="51[d]">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Abt">Abt</ref> 51[d]</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="51[d]" corresp="#wit-h">ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Abt_51-d.lnote.oe.2"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> siþþan gehwylc: scilling.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#oliver" n="48.3" corresp="#wit-h">And þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> siþþan gehwylc, scilling.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#oliver" corresp="#wit-h">And [for] each of the others, a shilling.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">and beyond that 1 shilling [shall be paid as compensation] for each tooth.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Abt_51-d.lnote.de.4" rend="supplied"/> dann dahinter jeder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Abt_51-d.lnote.de.5"/> [1] Schilling.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">and then each one behind that, [1] shilling.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Abt_51-d.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">6</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geändert in</hi> and</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to and</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">One footnote serves two places on p. 6: Abt 51 and 56.</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Abt_51-d.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">11</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">[setze diese Notenzahl über ‘und’] H’s Korrektor modernisiert häufig <hi rend="italic">ð,</hi> das vor Nasalen im 9. Jh. meist stand (Sievers <hi rend="italic">Gramm.</hi> 65), in <hi rend="italic">a</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">[put this note number over ‘and’] H’s corrector frequently modernises <hi rend="italic">ð</hi>, which in the 9th cent. mostly stood before nasals (Sievers <hi rend="italic">Gramm.</hi> 65), to <hi rend="italic">a</hi></seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">Not printed in vol. I; Liebermann: "setze diese Notenzahl über ‘und’" (III p. 11).</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Abt_51-d.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">11</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">gehwilc</hi> Lesefehler; die 20 übrigen sind die Backenzähne</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">gehwilc</hi> is a misreading; the remaining 20 are the molars</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">Vol. I prints no ⁴ in this clause before ⁵ (see note 4).</note></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
